# Everything under data/raw/ is derived: the Geofabrik download itself, the
# pyosmium prefilters, and the boundary/line caches built from them. All of it
# is regenerated by `python network.py prepare` plus the analysis subcommands,
# and national_lines.gpkg alone is 115 MB - over GitHub's 100 MB per-file
# limit. The finished artefacts in data/ are committed instead, which is what
# lets `python plots.py national` redraw the map without any of this.
data/raw/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# workshop
.venv/
graph-workshop/data/session1_state.npz
graph-workshop/data/cache/

# Profiles are derived from data/raw/weather and are 50 MB an hour-year;
# rebuild them with `python profiles.py build` rather than committing them.
data/profiles/

# LaTeX build artefacts
docs/report/*.aux
docs/report/*.log
docs/report/*.out
docs/report/*.toc
